// ============================================================================
// ORDERS DOMAIN - owned by Member 2
// Quotes, negotiation, orders, milestones, quality control, payments,
// cancellations and ratings.
//
// Integration contract with core.prisma (Member 1):
//   - Quote        -> invitationId (JobInvitation), jobId (Job), workshopId (Workshop)
//                     Only workshops with an INVITED/ACCEPTED invitation may quote.
//   - Order        -> jobId @unique (one order per job), buyerId (User), workshopId (Workshop)
//                     Creating an order sets Job.status = AWARDED.
//   - Milestone    -> orderId
//   - Inspection   -> orderId, inspectorId (User with role INSPECTOR)
//   - Payment      -> orderId (simulated)
//   - Rating       -> orderId @unique, workshopId, buyerId
//                     After insert, update Workshop.rating (running average),
//                     Workshop.ratingCount and Workshop.totalCompletedJobs.
//
// Prisma requires both sides of a relation: when you add a model that points
// at a core model, also add the back-relation field in core.prisma (marked
// with "Member 2: add back-relations here").
//
// Migrations: pull latest `backend` branch BEFORE running `npm run db:migrate`
// so migration folders stay linear.
// ============================================================================
